</section>

<h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom Line</h2>

<p>Véra is the jailbreak the Kindle community has been waiting for: root access on the current generation of Amazon's e-readers, on the latest firmware, with no computer in sight. For EPUB readers, it turns the newest Kindles into open reading devices — KOReader on a Paperwhite 6 or Colorsoft renders your Calibre library natively, free of Amazon's conversion layer.</p>

<p>It is not for everyone. The Scribe Colorsoft is still unsupported, Amazon can patch the exploit at any time, and the setup demands careful attention to model and firmware compatibility. But if you have been holding off on buying a new Kindle because you wanted EPUB freedom, Véra just removed the last big objection — and your DRM-free library, organized in Calibre, will be ready the day you root.</p>
